Code of Practice for Packing of Cargo Transport Units — IMO, ILO and UNECE (@cs-ctu: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_4YS4SQPG6WKX5TWAF48M0VV9X1
IMO/ILO/UNECE. Code of Practice for Packing of Cargo Transport Units, CTU Code, endorsed 2014. [Official code, searchable reading and downloads](https://unece.org/transport/intermodal-transport/imoilounece-code-practice-packing-cargo-transport-units-ctu-code).

Read the complete code and relevant annexes for the intermodal project: responsibilities, selecting/inspecting the unit, packing, securing, dangerous goods, receiving and training. Distinguish the separately issued informative material, MSC.1/Circ.1498, from the code itself. Translate a package list into a physically plausible load and receiving operation.

The official scope, 2014 endorsement and access routes were checked on 29 October 2026. UNECE describes the code as non-mandatory global guidance; route-specific adopted rules still need their own evidence. Some download paths ask short access questions. Publication/component rights are retained and no universal open licence or inspection of all downloadable language versions is claimed. All content stays external.

**Return:** [Chemical supply sources — books, methods, complete cases and research](../Sources.lingua#r_76J82CV79QKHQ2CSCT63MFYJYN).
